nodecode-adwave is a rewrite of AdwaveInc's AdwaveInc/adwave-agent-plugin:

  https://github.com/AdwaveInc/adwave-agent-plugin
  commit 0b5ab18aa6ebcde1a33f7dcd399a8c07cebf342c
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Adwave (LICENSE)

The plugin was a portable Agent Plugins v1 package with no code of its own:
plugin.json, mcp.json and five more platform manifests, all declaring the
hosted MCP server at https://waverunner.adwave.com/api/mcp (Streamable HTTP,
OAuth or an API key), and one skill, skills/adwave/SKILL.md, that taught a
model when to advertise through Adwave and how to spend safely. This rewrite
speaks that server's MCP wire itself, in Common Lisp over nlk:http --
initialize, the Mcp-Session-Id, tools/list, tools/call, an answer that is
either a JSON object or a one-event stream -- so every tool the server offers
is reachable by the name the server gives it, behind two tools, adwave_tools
and adwave_call. The skill, whole, is the manual topic (help :adwave) and its
one-line summary in every request, and the rule it stated in prose -- a clear
yes, with the amount said first, before any call that spends -- is enforced by
adwave_call, which refuses a tool not marked read-only until confirmed is
true. What was left out: the manifests, which the cell contract replaces with
a section and a declaration; the OAuth browser flow, which the shipped mcp
cell already owns, so this cell reuses that sign-in or a pasted key; and a
purpose-named tool for each of the server's tools, because the repository
carries no schema for them and a list restated here would go stale. Nothing of
the original is vendored: there was no code to vendor.
